{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"insectean-islandlike-alpaca","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Context\n\nDiscovered while fixing 79d6 (financial-maroon-toucan, Gerrit 1658), which unguarded the region env so every live-LLM matrix arm resolves a Bedrock region.\n\nThe remaining half of the same asymmetry is NOT fixed: in .github/workflows/external-integration.yml the OIDC step 'Configure AWS credentials' is gated `if: matrix.provider == 'bedrock'`. But live-LLM modules may pin a bedrock model whichever arm runs them — tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py pins `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`. So on the anthropic and openai arms those cells now have a region but still no AWS credential, and may fail on credential resolution instead.\n\n# Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — Decide and record the intended behavior: either (a) bedrock-pinned modules are excluded from non-bedrock arms (marker/skip, so the arm is honest about what it covers), or (b) the OIDC step runs on every arm so bedrock-pinned cells can execute anywhere.\n- [ ] AC2 — Whichever is chosen, a non-bedrock arm never reports green while silently skipping a bedrock-pinned module (the llm-live-canary contract holds).\n- [ ] AC3 — docs/ci-provider-matrix.md states the decision.","id":"4f74-eeae-4e91-41ca","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bedrock-pinned live-LLM modules lack AWS credentials on non-bedrock arms"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786558283057498001,"uuid":"a2fb7810-2342-4150-b60e-cac05382dde9"}